<title>USA: Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Iowa-So Minn hogs estimate Wednesday 100,000 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said Wednesday's estimated interior Iowa and southern Minnesota hog receipts were 100,000 head, compared with 111,000 a week ago and 98,000 a year ago. Estimates include generally about 65 percent Carcass Base Hogs. Barrows and gilts $1.00 higher compared midsession Tuesday. Trade slow for good demand and light to moderate offerings.</p>
<p>				 Country		    Plants</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>220-260 lbs	    55.50 -56.50	   56.50 -57.50</p>
<p>few			55.00  57.00	   56.00  58.00</p>
<p>US 1-3   46-49% Carcass Base Lean*</p>
<p>260-280 lbs	    54.50 -56.50	   55.00 -57.50</p>
<p>US 2-4   43-49% Carcass Base Lean</p>
<p>280-300 lbs	    54.50 -56.50	   55.00 -57.50</p>
<p>Sows:  mostly steady to 1.00 higher.</p>
